
# FUSESAFE - Material Properties

## 1. Material Selection

Selected material: Aluminium 2024-T3

Status: PROVISIONAL - Educational model only.

Material form: Aluminium sheet
Assumed skin thickness: 2 mm

## 2. Material Properties

| Property | Symbol | Value | Unit |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Young's Modulus | E | 73100 | MPa |
| Poisson's Ratio | nu | 0.33 | Dimensionless |
| Density | rho | 2780 | kg/m^3 |
| Tensile Yield Strength | sigma_y | 345 | MPa |

## 3. Design Requirements

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---:|
| Required Factor of Safety | 2 |
| Skin thickness | 2 mm |
| Pressure difference | 55 kPa |
| Fuselage radius | 2000 mm |

## 4. Preliminary Strength Calculation

Allowable stress based on yield:

sigma_allowable = sigma_y / FoS

sigma_allowable = 345 / 2

sigma_allowable = 172.5 MPa

## 5. Material Data Limitations

The listed values are representative preliminary
properties, not certified design allowables.

Actual properties depend on sheet thickness,
product form, material specification and orientation.

A thickness-specific manufacturer datasheet must
be obtained before finalising the material definition.

## 6. References

1. MatWeb - Aluminum 2024-T3:
https://www.matweb.com/search/datasheet.aspx?MatGUID=57483b4d782940faaf12964a1821fb61

2. NASA Technical Report - Mechanical Properties
of 2024-T3 Aluminum Alloy:
